/-! #### `A26-1-N` — the count -/

/-- **`A26-1-N`, the count of the relabelled Fourier circles: nine.** The list `R` of nine pairs
of permutations — a coset representative of `P` in `Perm (Fin 4)` for the rows and one for the
columns — has (i) nine entries, pairwise distinct; (ii) for distinct `r, r' ∈ R` the circle of `r`
is not contained in the circle of `r'`: at the exhibited unit parameter the relabelled tuple is
phase-equivalent to no tuple of the other circle at any unit parameter, the inequivalence read
through a core coordinate `((0, 0, i), (0, 0, j))` of act 24's feature map; (iii) every relabelled
circle equals the circle of some `r ∈ R` as a set of classes, both inclusions, through the
decomposition of each permutation as a representative followed by an element of `P` and the
stabilizer theorem `pred_stab`. The count is `9 = 576 / 64`; it enters no label. -/
